```
This breaks at the *first* null character, effectively truncating the string at the first null. To fix this, I need to find the *true length* of the string by scanning backwards from the end to find the last non-null character. Then, I loop from 0 to that true length, checking `Py_UNICODE_ISALPHA`. If any character is not alpha (including nulls in the middle), `is_alpha` becomes 0.

